{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩-⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98216/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-96943"] :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection/64e0147bf6e9832aa0bbc8ff8058cb483ca21d1ab5b774bb71699643a2ba78cd" :answer/id #uuid "3067398b-d785-5d98-80cd-aa63c7609821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i-6\\,j-9\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection/d48cdf0fde04cd66941cf2cd400ee3273d32daabeabc9c656b00765b999950d5" :answer/id #uuid "705cd188-90a0-5b87-918e-7db50dcaa4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+6\\,j+9\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection/91cefff2ae84b9b4b342c4c2fa8d0e7fced1f5727b4b62550208874bc33af4d0" :answer/id #uuid "e2e4e500-a6d6-5e1c-b1ba-2d1d5c878b73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i-6\\,j+8\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection/583e6615d7d217e88adba48df5049bd2e3df7e6138fa5c6fecce3d2bb6de34ed" :answer/id #uuid "aa14e4e8-7f9c-5bfd-a580-3d78072fb500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection/1e12ab2010dbb1e77986a7ad82a1cb3c1cce2a0c19de04d3900030ecdc20fb5b" :answer/id #uuid "a52d6fe4-983d-5fc5-abfa-852967224537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-9\\,j-8\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa14558-5238-5a43-90a3-55a974287e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98279/selection/583e6615d7d217e88adba48df5049bd2e3df7e6138fa5c6fecce3d2bb6de34ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-98279/selection/64e0147bf6e9832aa0bbc8ff8058cb483ca21d1ab5b774bb71699643a2ba78cd" "q-98279/selection/d48cdf0fde04cd66941cf2cd400ee3273d32daabeabc9c656b00765b999950d5" "q-98279/selection/91cefff2ae84b9b4b342c4c2fa8d0e7fced1f5727b4b62550208874bc33af4d0" "q-98279/selection/583e6615d7d217e88adba48df5049bd2e3df7e6138fa5c6fecce3d2bb6de34ed" "q-98279/selection/1e12ab2010dbb1e77986a7ad82a1cb3c1cce2a0c19de04d3900030ecdc20fb5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98279" :question/id #uuid "e6eb25e4-3fa7-5a49-963f-966694cb971b" :question/math-academy-id "q-98279" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-2\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-2\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-6+8)i-(3-12)j+(-4+12)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "98f31c75-cfb3-5078-8017-f781be5519fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "18056e48-a148-5750-a397-9f71b2e634b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "bea486b9-ce9d-53ff-bcad-d7b8795a8a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f6ba3181-f272-5b10-a279-b05934db8da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3ce26c67-cfda-52e4-9f57-c8ed7a3267e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f96b68bd-58a7-540b-8429-0e37f49d2bcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32300/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-32300/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-32300/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-32300/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-32300/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-32300/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32300" :question/id #uuid "418288b0-73e1-53ba-989d-6a1076766b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-32300" :question/problem "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k,$ \n$c=i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}+u-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $u=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32300/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection/226412779b30470b6407e074c20faac9f38dcef5e3618424c4518566a1dd0900" :answer/id #uuid "b50fbe45-6032-5e10-b724-973d548d8370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection/59ea3a9d4275768c45175c3d1716461ab9fbdc66cd258482de76898e0a85cce4" :answer/id #uuid "e1442c01-034a-509a-867f-993ff3269333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection/9089aefeda70249e88940c7b16f12f3ea57fd9d6f9c3fd57d03a8ecdf8270ed1" :answer/id #uuid "3c997252-5dbb-5a11-a403-e265b4d7d938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection/674a033d474465d9d9f0df4493c45bcc048338c813d1c1fef462595179d3fcd3" :answer/id #uuid "a7ecd1ce-9d01-5ca4-bf64-e0e38d733f32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection/49ab6cb24d422dffbcc0aad52b1608a4e8bab269f15459dac6e9e4364408b036" :answer/id #uuid "9f064df7-0264-5f56-9529-d5fae71bc4c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "071e7d83-27cc-575e-9c4e-8f49dcfa6913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32511/selection/674a033d474465d9d9f0df4493c45bcc048338c813d1c1fef462595179d3fcd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-32511/selection/226412779b30470b6407e074c20faac9f38dcef5e3618424c4518566a1dd0900" "q-32511/selection/59ea3a9d4275768c45175c3d1716461ab9fbdc66cd258482de76898e0a85cce4" "q-32511/selection/9089aefeda70249e88940c7b16f12f3ea57fd9d6f9c3fd57d03a8ecdf8270ed1" "q-32511/selection/674a033d474465d9d9f0df4493c45bcc048338c813d1c1fef462595179d3fcd3" "q-32511/selection/49ab6cb24d422dffbcc0aad52b1608a4e8bab269f15459dac6e9e4364408b036"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32511" :question/id #uuid "c3f231af-a109-5d91-91bf-559d88bb159f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32511" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})+{e}^{-2}\\cdot {e}^{2}-{e}^{2}\\cdot (2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =e-1+1-2e+3 \\\\  & =3-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32511/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32511"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection/b6e91c612029b882f4c05b67ffbc7f6d3247068ba7511ae9df490165ec733d65" :answer/id #uuid "ccaa5a2b-a015-56c6-ac37-5031c36333b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i-6j-4k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection/190c6feefcf0a0d0583ca233e9701b549b6ff06a4c161b6cb20129246fd21fcf" :answer/id #uuid "06e1a8bd-192a-5d8c-911a-e177dfb7ce9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2i-2j+4k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection/6d1d27638e0b5d7db2933f57cd6664924968f11a9396678d4d1b091e71065b15" :answer/id #uuid "b11c2512-97aa-5321-8629-5246aea9bddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i+2j-4k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection/b452f9ed24b1dea2505c0f9a4cc2c14979a75bb5b644a4caa2361c269b4c0b5f" :answer/id #uuid "a7df66a0-c3b2-540a-abf1-e56481e17e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+6j+2k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection/626217bf16e26b73845c40d39e4b5a427cf8f2f3c72b691c30c67fc15c38ca12" :answer/id #uuid "8574fde5-fb29-5ac6-8416-2de97bb2fc76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4i-6j+2k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6eede9-d55d-59ed-8257-0f817d1476ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32522/selection/b6e91c612029b882f4c05b67ffbc7f6d3247068ba7511ae9df490165ec733d65" :answer-field/choices ["q-32522/selection/b6e91c612029b882f4c05b67ffbc7f6d3247068ba7511ae9df490165ec733d65" "q-32522/selection/190c6feefcf0a0d0583ca233e9701b549b6ff06a4c161b6cb20129246fd21fcf" "q-32522/selection/6d1d27638e0b5d7db2933f57cd6664924968f11a9396678d4d1b091e71065b15" "q-32522/selection/b452f9ed24b1dea2505c0f9a4cc2c14979a75bb5b644a4caa2361c269b4c0b5f" "q-32522/selection/626217bf16e26b73845c40d39e4b5a427cf8f2f3c72b691c30c67fc15c38ca12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32522" :question/id #uuid "b190b78e-5c96-53ca-a8be-8f4dce1bb987" :question/math-academy-id "q-32522" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,i+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i+j-k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+j-k)\\times (4\\,i+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2+4)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =2i-6j-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32522/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32522"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" :answer/id #uuid "a742960a-291b-5f6d-941d-8feed273b383" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" :answer/id #uuid "38ad5ce5-63f9-5dfd-b1ef-115d17cbdbe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" :answer/id #uuid "bb969a54-095c-511a-a27d-70d47aef14ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" :answer/id #uuid "1ee64a05-e0f5-5a3c-abd0-0c6145a18443" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection/087d6195df78ac19ad68ba3746305a749712648815fc499a6add393278e08471" :answer/id #uuid "2ace370e-56c0-5576-8e83-abd125e2df87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "08f27964-0fa7-52e8-96b6-1ab2a9f1e3b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129292/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" :answer-field/choices ["q-129292/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" "q-129292/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" "q-129292/selection/5a1fe28b022029f27455dc36a9cc0dbfd0eced1186649091706824f56db6ba8d" "q-129292/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" "q-129292/selection/087d6195df78ac19ad68ba3746305a749712648815fc499a6add393278e08471"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129292" :question/id #uuid "d095f207-55b2-50fd-ba56-af11025422d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-129292" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{2}\\,i-\\,j+e\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{-1}\\,i+j+k.$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{-1}\\,i+j+k)\\cdot ({e}^{2}\\,i-\\,j+e\\,k) \\\\  & =e-1+e \\\\  & =2e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129292/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3019"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8688"] :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3020"] :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3021"] :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
